# Line-ending policy — keep every text file LF in the repo AND in the working
# tree on every OS.
#
# Why this exists: GitHub's Windows runners check code out with Git's
# core.autocrlf default, which rewrites LF -> CRLF in the working tree. Biome's
# formatter expects LF (biome.json formatter.lineEnding defaults to lf), so on
# the windows-latest CI leg every file is flagged with a stray carriage return
# and `pnpm run lint` fails on 1000+ files. `eol=lf` overrides core.autocrlf, so
# the checkout is LF on Windows too and Biome sees what macOS/Linux see.
#
# After changing this file, run `git add --renormalize .` once to apply it to
# already-tracked files.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets — never normalize line endings, never diff as text.
*.png binary
*.svg binary
*.mp4 binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.wasm binary
*.gz binary
*.node binary
